# Build context hygiene.
#
# Patterns here match from the context root, so a bare `node_modules`
# excludes the one at the top and *not* apps/web/node_modules — which is
# 816 MB, uploaded to Fly's remote builder on every deploy, for an image
# that contains no JavaScript at all. Hence the globs.
.git
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.next
**/*.log

# Local development state: a SQLite database and a local object store.
apps/api/.storage
apps/api/dev.db

# Benchmark and acceptance output. The corpus itself stays — it is small,
# and it is what `make bench` grades against.
benchmarks/out
benchmarks/ab/out
benchmarks/acceptance/out

# The web app is a Vercel project; neither image serves it.
apps/web
